NAME
       xfs_db - examine and debug the inside of an XFS file system

SYNOPSIS
       xfs_db [-r] [-c COMMAND] DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       xfs_db is a low-level tool for XFS experts. It reads (and can change)
       the structures inside an XFS file system: superblocks, inodes,
       directory blocks. Ordinary administration never needs it; a wrong
       write can destroy the file system. Use xfs_info, xfs_admin and
       xfs_repair instead.

OPTIONS
       -r     Read only.

       -c COMMAND
              Run COMMAND and exit, for example -c 'sb 0' -c print.

SEE ALSO
       xfs_info(8), xfs_admin(8), xfs_repair(8)
